body: "# recursive-cuddling-blossom.md — Final Closure (2026-06-09)\n\n## Status: COMPLETE — all gate-bearing + functional dimensions green\n\n## Reconciliation (ground truth, FACT [1.0])\nPrior sessions had already delivered the bulk of the plan; this session reconciled\nin loco and closed the residual gaps.\n\n| Workstream | Items | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| WS1 A01 extraction | S-11 saga / S-12 rl / S-13 CEG seam | DONE (deployed; facade `touring_hooks::{saga,agentic_rl}` resolves; 2 external consumers) |\n| WS2 E-W2 benchmark | S-21/22/23 MiniMax-M3 multi-repo | DONE (harness + dataset touring-multiswe-rust.jsonl + 4 reports) |\n| WS3 gaps | S-31/32/33/34/35/36 | DONE (this session closed S-31, S-33, S-36) |\n| WS4 | S-41 checkpoint / S-42 deploy | DONE |\n\n## Closed this session\n- **S-31** ARCHITECTURE.md:3 header drift: `36 crates|472,614 LOC` → `38 crates|477,646 LOC src / 545,366 workspace | 13,321 test fns`; wave label → A01. `sync_metrics.py --check` now OK (declared=38, measured=39, within 5% tol).\n- **S-33** README.md:128 footer: `hooks: 198` → `218` (verified via `ALL_DAEMON_HOOK_NAMES.len() == 218` assertion at hook_registry.rs:1967).\n- **S-36** N01 fold: relocated 12 `cli_handlers*.rs` (hub→`cli/handlers/dispatch.rs`, 9 satellites, 2 `#[cfg(test)]` submodules gate_tests/tests) from `touring-hooks/src/` top-level into `cli/handlers/` via `#[path]`. Module paths PRESERVED (`touring_hooks::cli_handlers_*` unchanged) → zero facade indirection, zero external-API break.\n\n## S-36 decision rationale\nPlan premise (\"N01 needs the fold\") was measurement-invalidated: file_size_gate PASSES,\n`cli/` already grouped 42 modules, and `cli_handlers_mcp` exposes ctx_* consumed cross-crate\nby touring-server (20 refs). Gabriel chose the full fold; executed via `#[path]` (the plan's\nsanctioned low-risk variant) rather than move+facade, so no indirection was added — the only\nchange is physical file location; the public module namespace is byte-for-byte identical.\n\n## Validation (proof discipline — Hard Rule #9)\n- `cargo check --workspace` EXIT 0 (incl. touring-server cross-crate consumer)\n- `cargo test --no-run -p touring-hooks` EXIT 0 (moved #[cfg(test)] submodules compile)\n- `cargo check -p touring-hooks --features tantivy-fts` EXIT 0 (tantivy-gated ctx_* in cli/handlers/mcp.rs)\n- `wiring cycles` = 0 (DAG acyclic)\n- `file_size_gate --check` EXIT 0 / `sync_metrics --check` EXIT 0 / `wiring_integrity` 0 cycles\n- Reindex: 25 stale top-level cli_handlers paths purged; symbol DB now points to cli/handlers/\n- REGRA #0: orphan count 3980 unchanged (relocation creates no new pub symbols)\n\n## Deploy (S-42)\n- `update-touring` EXIT 0 (release LTO 7m03s + dual-target symlinks)\n- REGRA #3 hit: update-touring \"skip start\" left daemon PID 119089 on deleted inode;\n  resolved via `touring daemon-ctl restart` (REGRA #19) → PID 125864 on fresh non-deleted binary\n- `touring doctor -j` 5/6 ok (wiring_diagnostic=warning pre-existing/non-blocking)\n\n## Lessons persisted\n- `#[path]` fold > move+facade when module paths must survive for cross-crate callers (no indirection).\n- REGRA #3 recurs whenever a session hook auto-spawns the daemon mid-rebuild; `daemon-ctl restart` is the canonical fix (never pkill).\n- A plan item's premise can be invalidated by measurement (file_size_gate) between authoring and execution — verify gates before mechanically executing.\n"
